    "text": "For a first order reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>, the rate constant, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The time required for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>67</mn><mo>%</mo></math> completion of reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> times the half life of reaction. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&nbsp;is Nearest integer) (Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4771</mn></math>)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "16",
  "solution": {
